---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'MyTrips';
const outcome =
	'An itinerary maker for spontaneous travelers. I designed it from scratch as my Pratt capstone in 2018, my first app from zero to one, and later redesigned it on my own.';
const proto = 'https://mytrips-prototype-37ptf5c3o-caseylflood-gmailcoms-projects.vercel.app/';
const b = '/mytrips';

const stats = [
	{ v: '−94%', l: 'time to share a trip' },
	{ v: '93%', l: 'of testers used the auto timeline' },
	{ v: '~30', l: 'research and testing participants' },
];

const insights = [
	['Sharing is the goal', 'People wanted to pass a trip along to friends. They stalled when sharing meant rebuilding it.'],
	['Memory fades fast', 'Within a week, most details were gone: scattered across the camera roll, maps and receipts.'],
	['No planners here', 'Journals want a diary and itinerary apps want a plan. Neither fits a trip that’s still happening.'],
];

const colors = [
	{ n: 'Navy', h: '#1B263B', use: 'Headers, navigation' },
	{ n: 'Sky', h: '#73C2FB', use: 'Primary actions' },
	{ n: 'Coral', h: '#FF6F61', use: 'Start a trip' },
	{ n: 'Mist', h: '#EDEDED', use: 'Surfaces' },
	{ n: 'Lemon', h: '#F4D35E', use: 'Highlights' },
];

const flows = [
	{ src: 'sitemap.webp', t: 'Sitemap', d: 'Four tabs: My trips, Friends, Explore, Settings.' },
	{ src: 'user-flow.webp', t: 'User flow', d: 'Travel Mode on or off decides where you land.' },
	{ src: 'journey-map.webp', t: 'Journey map', d: 'Before, during and after the trip.' },
	{ src: 'system-flow.webp', t: 'System flow', d: 'What the app stores, syncs and shares.' },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={outcome} progress>
	<div class="mt">
		<section class="mt-hero">
			<div class="shell">
				<a class="back" href="/work">← All work</a>
				<p class="mt-eyebrow">MyTrips · Pratt capstone, 2018 · Redesign, 2024</p>
				<h1>Share the trip, <em>skip the homework.</em></h1>
				<p class="mt-lede">{outcome}</p>
				<ul class="mt-meta">
					<li>Solo designer</li>
					<li>iOS · 0 → 1</li>
					<li>Research, IA, UI, testing</li>
				</ul>
				<ul class="mt-stats">
					{stats.map((s) => <li><strong>{s.v}</strong><span>{s.l}</span></li>)}
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-note">Results are from moderated user testing, not a shipped product.</p>
				<p><a class="mt-btn" href={proto} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the live prototype ↗&#xFE0E;</a></p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- 2018 -->
		<section class="mt-sec">
			<div class="shell">
				<p class="mt-kicker"><span class="mt-dot"></span>2018 · Pratt capstone</p>
				<h2>My first app, from an empty file.</h2>
				<p class="mt-p">
					Friends ask for recommendations the moment you’re home, but spontaneous trips never get written down. I wanted to know why sharing a trip felt like homework, then design my way out of it.
				</p>

				<figure class="mt-fig">
					<img src={`${b}/empathy-wall.webp`} alt="Building the empathy map with classmates at Pratt: says, thinks, does, feels" data-zoom loading="lazy" />
					<figcaption>An empathy map built from interviews: what travelers say, think, do and feel.</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<ol class="mt-insights">
					{insights.map(([t, d], i) => <li><span>0{i + 1}</span><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p></li>)}
				</ol>

				<div class="mt-two">
					<figure class="mt-fig">
						<img src={`${b}/card-sort.webp`} alt="A participant grouping cards on the floor during a moderated open card sort" data-zoom loading="lazy" />
						<figcaption>A moderated open card sort. Photos, sharing and the camera kept landing together, so they became one flow.</figcaption>
					</figure>
					<figure class="mt-fig">
						<video src="/journey/usertesting.mp4" poster="/journey/usertesting-poster.jpg" muted loop playsinline autoplay preload="none" aria-label="Card sorts and prototype testing sessions"></video>
						<figcaption>Testing the prototype with travelers, in person.</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>

				<aside class="mt-callout">
					<p class="mt-callout__k">The decision that mattered</p>
					<p class="mt-callout__t">Don’t ask people to review a whole trip at once.</p>
					<p>
						That’s where testers dropped off. So the app builds the timeline from photos and location in the background, and asks for a quick review each day. Sharing becomes one tap at the end.
					</p>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Results -->
		<section class="mt-band">
			<div class="shell">
				<p class="mt-kicker mt-kicker--light">In testing</p>
				<div class="mt-result">
					<div class="mt-bars" aria-hidden="true">
						<div><span style="--w:100%"></span><b>~90 min</b><small>Rebuilding a trip by hand</small></div>
						<div><span style="--w:5.5%"></span><b>~5 min</b><small>Reviewing the timeline MyTrips built</small></div>
					</div>
					<p class="mt-result__big"><strong>−94%</strong> time to share a trip</p>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-band__p">93% of testers used the automatic timeline instead of building one. Privacy mattered as much as speed: people shared more when they could see and correct what would leave their phone.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Redesign -->
		<section class="mt-sec">
			<div class="shell">
				<p class="mt-kicker"><span class="mt-dot mt-dot--sky"></span>2024 · The redesign</p>
				<h2>Same problem, sharper tools.</h2>
				<p class="mt-p">
					Years later I came back to it on my own, with five years of product work behind me. I kept the core lesson (review a day, not a trip), and rebuilt the structure, the interface and a small design system around a new idea: Travel Mode.
				</p>

				<figure class="mt-fig mt-fig--flush">
					<img src={`${b}/hero-phones.webp`} alt="Two MyTrips screens: a daily review prompt in Travel Mode, and a profile with published trips" data-zoom loading="lazy" />
					<figcaption>Travel Mode drafts each day from your photos and location. You confirm it, then publish.</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<h3 class="mt-h3">Structure first</h3>
				<div class="mt-grid">
					{flows.map((f) => (
						<figure class="mt-tile">
							<img src={`${b}/${f.src}`} alt={f.t} data-zoom loading="lazy" />
							<figcaption><b>{f.t}</b>{f.d}</figcaption>
						</figure>
					))}
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-h3">Wireframes, with my own review notes</h3>
				<figure class="mt-fig">
					<img src={`${b}/wireframes.webp`} alt="Grayscale MyTrips wireframes with annotation notes on published vs. unpublished trips, bottom sheets and accessibility" data-zoom loading="lazy" />
					<figcaption>Questions I left for myself: one active trip or many? What happens with dozens of trips? Do bottom sheets work with a screen reader?</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<h3 class="mt-h3">A small design system</h3>
				<div class="mt-ds">
					<ul class="mt-swatches">
						{colors.map((c) => (
							<li>
								<span style={`--c:${c.h}`}></span>
								<b>{c.n}</b>
								<code>{c.h}</code>
								<small>{c.use}</small>
							</li>
						))}
					</ul>
					<div class="mt-type">
						<p class="mt-type__h1">Heading 1 · 32 bold</p>
						<p class="mt-type__h2">Heading 2 · 24 bold</p>
						<p class="mt-type__b">Body · 16 regular. Inter, on an 8-point grid, with 44px touch targets.</p>
						<div class="mt-btns">
							<span class="mt-b mt-b--p">Save</span>
							<span class="mt-b mt-b--c">Start a new trip</span>
							<span class="mt-b mt-b--s">Learn more</span>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<figure class="mt-fig mt-fig--flush">
					<img src={`${b}/screens.webp`} alt="Nine MyTrips screens, from onboarding through Travel Mode, friends’ trips, explore and profile" data-zoom loading="lazy" />
					<figcaption>The full flow: onboarding, Travel Mode, daily review, friends, explore and profile.</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-sec mt-sec--last">
			<div class="shell">
				<h2>What it taught me</h2>
				<ol class="mt-insights">
					<li><span>01</span><h3>Design for real behavior</h3><p>The best idea came from watching people quit, not from the brief.</p></li>
					<li><span>02</span><h3>Automate, then let people correct</h3><p>Trust came from seeing and fixing what the app guessed.</p></li>
					<li><span>03</span><h3>Revisit your own work</h3><p>Redesigning my first app showed me how much my structure and systems thinking had grown.</p></li>
				</ol>
				<p class="mt-end">
					<a class="mt-btn" href={proto} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the live prototype ↗&#xFE0E;</a>
					<a class="mt-link" href="/journey#pratt">Back to my story →</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<dialog class="mt-lb" aria-label="Image viewer">
			<button class="mt-lb__x" aria-label="Close">×</button>
			<img alt="" />
		</dialog>
	</div>
</Base>

<script>
	const lb = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>('.mt-lb');
	const lbImg = lb?.querySelector('img');
	document.querySelectorAll<HTMLImageElement>('.mt img[data-zoom]').forEach((img) => {
		img.addEventListener('click', () => {
			if (!lb || !lbImg) return;
			lbImg.src = img.currentSrc || img.src;
			lbImg.alt = img.alt;
			lb.showModal();
		});
	});
	lb?.addEventListener('click', () => lb.close());
</script>

<style>
	.mt { --navy: #1b263b; --sky: #73c2fb; --coral: #ff6f61; --mt-ac: var(--navy); --mt-btn: var(--navy); --mt-btn-ink: #fff; }
	:global([data-theme='dark']) .mt { --mt-ac: var(--sky); --mt-btn: var(--sky); --mt-btn-ink: #0d1424; }
	.mt-hero { padding: 3rem 0 3.5rem; background: linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--sky) 16%, var(--bg)), var(--bg)); }
	.mt-eyebrow, .mt-kicker { font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
	.mt-hero h1 { font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.02; margin: 0; max-width: 16ch; }
	.mt-hero h1 em { color: var(--mt-ac); font-style: italic; }
	.mt-lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 40rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem; }
	.mt-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
	.mt-meta li { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 99px; padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem; font-size: 0.85rem; background: var(--paper); }
	.mt-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--line); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; overflow: hidden; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; max-width: 44rem; }
	.mt-stats li { background: var(--paper); padding: 1rem 1.1rem; }
	.mt-stats strong { display: block; font-family: var(--display); font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1; color: var(--mt-ac); }
	.mt-stats span { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
	.mt-note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0.6rem 0 1.5rem; }
	.mt-btn { display: inline-block; background: var(--mt-btn); color: var(--mt-btn-ink); padding: 0.7rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 99px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.92rem; }
	.mt-link { margin-left: 1rem; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }

	.mt-sec { padding: 4rem 0; }
	.mt-sec--last { padding-bottom: 5rem; }
	.mt-sec h2 { font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); line-height: 1.08; margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 20ch; }
	.mt-dot { width: 0.55rem; height: 0.55rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--coral); }
	.mt-dot--sky { background: var(--sky); }
	.mt-p { font-size: 1.08rem; max-width: 40rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2rem; }
	.mt-h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 3rem 0 1rem; }

	.mt-fig { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
	.mt-fig img, .mt-fig video { width: 100%; display: block; border-radius: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--paper); }
	.mt-fig--flush img { border: 0; }
	.mt-fig figcaption, .mt-tile figcaption { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.6rem; }
	.mt img[data-zoom] { cursor: zoom-in; }
	.mt-two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
	.mt-two img, .mt-two video { aspect-ratio: 1; object-fit: cover; }

	.mt-insights { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 2rem 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
	.mt-insights li { background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem; }
	.mt-insights span { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
	.mt-insights h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0.3rem 0; }
	.mt-insights p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

	.mt-callout { margin-top: 2rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--coral); padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.25rem; max-width: 40rem; }
	.mt-callout__k { font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--coral); font-weight: 700; margin: 0; }
	.mt-callout__t { font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0.3rem 0; line-height: 1.15; }
	.mt-callout p:last-child { color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

	.mt-band { background: var(--navy); border-block: 1px solid var(--line); color: #fff; padding: 3.5rem 0; }
	.mt-kicker--light { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.65); margin-top: 0; }
	.mt-result { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: center; }
	.mt-bars { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
	.mt-bars div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 0.25rem 1rem; align-items: center; }
	.mt-bars span { grid-column: 1 / -1; height: 0.75rem; border-radius: 99px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
	.mt-bars span::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0 auto 0 0; width: var(--w); min-width: 0.75rem; border-radius: 99px; background: var(--coral); }
	.mt-bars div:last-child span::after { background: var(--sky); }
	.mt-bars small { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); grid-row: 2; grid-column: 1; }
	.mt-bars b { grid-row: 2; grid-column: 2; }
	.mt-result__big { margin: 0; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75); }
	.mt-result__big strong { display: block; font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem); line-height: 1; color: #fff; }
	.mt-band__p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75); max-width: 40rem; margin: 2rem 0 0; }

	.mt-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; }
	.mt-tile { margin: 0; }
	.mt-tile img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 0.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #fff; display: block; }
	.mt-tile b { display: block; color: var(--ink); }

	.mt-ds { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
	.mt-swatches { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
	.mt-swatches li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.25rem 4.5rem 5rem 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center; font-size: 0.88rem; }
	.mt-swatches span { width: 2.25rem; height: 2.25rem; border-radius: 0.6rem; background: var(--c); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.mt-swatches code { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted); }
	.mt-swatches small { color: var(--muted); }
	.mt-type { background: var(--navy); color: #fff; border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.4rem; font-family: 'Inter', var(--sans); }
	.mt-type p { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
	.mt-type__h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; }
	.mt-type__h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; }
	.mt-type__b { font-size: 0.95rem; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75); }
	.mt-btns { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
	.mt-b { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; height: 44px; padding: 0 1.1rem; border-radius: 24px; font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 600; }
	.mt-b--p { background: var(--sky); color: #fff; }
	.mt-b--c { background: var(--coral); color: #fff; }
	.mt-b--s { background: #ededed; color: var(--navy); }

	.mt-end { margin-top: 2rem; }

	.mt-lb { border: 0; padding: 0; background: transparent; max-width: 96vw; max-height: 94vh; }
	.mt-lb::backdrop { background: rgba(10, 12, 20, 0.85); }
	.mt-lb img { max-width: 96vw; max-height: 90vh; display: block; border-radius: 0.75rem; }
	.mt-lb__x { position: fixed; top: 1rem; right: 1rem; width: 2.5rem; height: 2.5rem; border-radius: 50%; border: 0; background: #fff; font-size: 1.4rem; cursor: pointer; }

	@media (max-width: 760px) {
		.mt-hero { padding: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem; }
		.mt-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; }
		.mt-stats li { padding: 0.8rem; }
		.mt-stats strong { font-size: 1.5rem; }
		.mt-stats span { font-size: 0.75rem; }
		.mt-sec { padding: 3rem 0; }
		.mt-insights, .mt-two, .mt-grid, .mt-ds, .mt-result { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.mt-swatches li { grid-template-columns: 2.25rem 4rem 1fr; }
		.mt-swatches small { display: none; }
		.mt-link { display: block; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
	}
</style>
